Fix `Argument of type SafeString' is not assignable to parameter of type 'string'` TS error when passing a `SafeString` to the flash message service methods:

```
this.flashMessages.success(htmlSafe('Success!'));
// Argument of type SafeString' is not assignable to parameter of type 'string'
```

[This ticket](https://github.com/adopted-ember-addons/ember-cli-flash/pull/149) added `SafeString` as a valid argument to the flash message methods, but currently the type for message is only a string.  This PR introduces a `Message` type for message arguments to include `SafeString` to align with that behaviour.
